src/
└── com.indianbazar
    ├── model            # All POJO classes (Product, User, etc.)
    ├── service          # Interfaces like ProductService, UserService
    ├── service.impl     # Implementations of the service interfaces
    ├── controller       # Menu-driven logic or console simulation (optional for now)
    └── main             # Main entry point to run and test the app

    

| Class Name | Purpose                                                    |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Product`  | Defines all product-related fields (id, name, price, etc.) |
| `User`     | Defines user fields like id, name, email, password, role   |


| Interface Name   | Purpose                                             |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `ProductService` | Declares methods for product operations             |
| `UserService`    | Declares methods for user registration, login, etc. |


| Class Name           | Purpose                                                              |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ProductServiceImpl` | Implements logic to store, update, delete products using collections |
| `UserServiceImpl`    | Implements user-related logic (register/login) using a Map or List   |


| Class Name       | Purpose                                                                              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `IndianBazarApp` | Entry point of the application with `main()` method to simulate product/user actions |




1. Backend Setup
Model Class: Product.java (with fields like id, name, description, price, imageUrl, category)

Repository: ProductRepository.java

Service & Impl: To fetch products by category

Controller: /api/products?category=Electronics

2. Database Sample Data
Add 10 sample records per category in product_inventory_db

We’ll use either data.sql or a Spring Boot initializer method to pre-populate.

3. Frontend
On clicking a category (e.g., "Electronics"), make a fetch call to /api/products?category=Electronics and render the data dynamically, including images.
